ting “No Filming Allowed” inside the 7-Eleven.\n- **No explicit visual cues** (e.g., store exit door, receipt in hand, or transition from inside to outside) that confirm they *just exited* the store.\n- However, **it is highly plausible** that they purchased the food from the 7-Eleven and are eating it outside — a common practice in Japan, especially with hot food items from convenience stores, which often lack seating or discourage lingering.\n- **Filming restrictions** inside convenience stores are **common in Japan**, especially for commercial or vlog-style productions, due to privacy policies and store regulations. While **not visually confirmed**, this is a **realistic and culturally plausible reason** for filming outside.\n\n---\n\n### 📌 **Conclusion:**\n\nWhile **there is no direct visual evidence** (like a sign or on-screen text) stating “filming is not allowed inside,” the combination of:\n\n- The hosts standing outside with food from the store,\n- No seating available nearby,\n- The cultural context of Japanese convenience stores (often no seating or discouraging eating inside),\n- And the common practice of vloggers filming outside stores due to filming restrictions,\n\n…makes **option B (“Because filming is not allowed inside the 711 convenience store”)** a **reasonable and plausible inference**.\n\n> ✅ **Therefore, the answer ‘2’ is CORRECT based on contextual plausibility and the provided criteria.**\n\n---\n\n**Final Answer: YES — Answer ‘2’ is correct.**'}], 'formatted_responses': ["\n=== Batch 0-30 (30 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KktLi3UifPY/frames/frame_0238.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KktLi3UifPY/frames/frame_0239.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KktLi3UifPY/frames/frame_0240.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KktLi3UifPY/frames/frame_0241.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KktLi3UifPY/frames/frame_0242.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/KktLi3UifPY/frames/frame_